{
  "dom_id": "step-e5817",
  "name": "Example: Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial",
  "problem": "The graph of a polynomial $Q(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13928579/assets/c6729ee13a704ce630586cd4cbdde5c67e55c03f65f1840b2ca1f2b6c38186f2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n\n- The degree of $Q(x)$ is odd.\n\n- The constant term is negative.",
  "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $Q(x)\\to\\infty$ as $x\\to-\\infty,$ and\n\n- $Q(x)\\to-\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty.$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $Q(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $Q(x)$ is negative.\n\nSo I is false, and II is true.\n\nLastly, note that the $y$-intercept is $0,$ which means that $Q(0)$ must be equal to $0,$ and therefore the constant term must be equal to $0.$ So, III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
